#  Math Class in Java



`Math` is a built-in utility class in Java that provides mathematical 
operations and functions.

Package:
java.lang.Math


Since it belongs to `java.lang`,
no import is required.


#  Important Point

All methods in Math class are: static

So we use: Math.methodName()

No object creation needed.


#  Commonly Used Methods

| Method        | Purpose               |
| ------------- | --------------------- |
| Math.max()    | Maximum value         |
| Math.min()    | Minimum value         |
| Math.sqrt()   | Square root           |
| Math.pow()    | Power                 |
| Math.abs()    | Absolute value        |
| Math.random() | Random number         |
| Math.ceil()   | Round upward          |
| Math.floor()  | Round downward        |
| Math.round()  | Round nearest integer |
| Math.cbrt()   | Cube root             |



#  Math.max()

Returns larger value.
Math.max(10, 20)



# Math.min()

Returns smaller value.

Math.min(5, 2)


# Math.sqrt()

Returns square root.

Math.sqrt(25)


#  Math.pow()

Returns power value.

Math.pow(2, 3)


# Math.abs()

Returns absolute positive value.

Math.abs(-10)

# Math.random()

Generates random number between: 0.0 to less than 1.0

# Example
Math.random()


#  Generate Random Integer
(int)(Math.random() * 100)

Generates: 0 to 99


# Math.ceil()
Rounds upward.

Math.ceil(5.2)

Output: 6.0


# Math.floor()
Rounds downward.
Math.floor(5.9)

Output:5.0


# Math.round()

Rounds nearest integer.

Math.round(5.6)

Output:6


