# Important Interview Point

Math class constructor is private:
private Math()

So: cannot create object

new Math(); ❌

Because Math is a utility class.

In Java, a utility class is a specialized class designed to provide a
collection of related static methods that perform generic tasks across an application.
Unlike standard classes, utility classes are not intended to be instantiated.